{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GNUns17yB34RDq8F1Decme","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D16, 2026-10-16)\n2\t\n3\tWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\n4\tid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n5\t`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n6\t`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n7\t\n8\t**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\n9\tregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\n10\twhen one exists but is not built yet).\n11\t**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\n12\tIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:82`: stdlib subset +\n13\t`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\n14\toletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\n15\tworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n16\t**Likelihood** reasoning: D9-D15 walked Windows binaries/installers/shortcuts/Office (PE -> PE version -> .NET -> MSI\n17\t-> LNK -> OOXML); the next steps are most plausibly other Windows DFIR artifacts and legacy-Office/CFB siblings,\n18\tplus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 added cross-file synthesis).\n19\t**D16 turned to e-mail** (`email.message_id` of one `.eml`; flavor \"replies, forwards, duplicates, reconstructed\n20\tmessages ... stable message identities\"). PE stayed three days (D9-11) with a deeper field each day, so D17-D19 most\n21\tplausibly ask deeper `email.*` fields (In-Reply-To / References / attachments / Received / auth) or a sibling mail\n22\tcontainer (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis question. GM fmt word is `email`, not `eml`.\n23\t\n24\t## 1. Atlas\n25\t\n26\t| # | Concept / field | Status | Recognition cues | Standard tool / lib + exact call | D16+ likelihood |\n27\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n28\t| 1 | Identity: filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | seen D1 (+D15 member roster) | any member; id stem names WHICH member | `hashlib.<algo>(b).hexdigest()`; `sha256sum` (I) | high -- every timed kit |\n29\t| 2 | `file.magic_prefix_hex_N` | seen D2 | first N bytes | `xxd -p -l 16` (I); `b[:N].hex()` | high (carry-over) |\n30\t| 3 | `text.utf8_bom_present` (utf16 sibling speculative) | seen D3 | `ef bb bf` / `ff fe` / `fe ff` | `b.startswith(codecs.BOM_UTF8)` | high (carry-over) |\n31\t| 4 | `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` | seen D4 | `ff d8 ff`; SOFn `ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc | segment walk; `identify -format %wx%h` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n32\t| 5 | `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` | seen D5 | `89 50 4e 47 0d 0a 1a 0a`; IHDR @12 | `struct.unpack('>II', b[16:24])`; `pngcheck -v` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n33\t| 6 | `pdf.header_version` | seen D6 | `%PDF-x.y` @0 | `b[5:8]`; `pdfinfo` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n34\t| 7 | `zip.eocd_total_entries` | seen D7 | `PK\\x05\\x06` last; u16 @+10 | struct; `7z l -slt` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n35\t| 8 | `zip.central_directory_member_names` (CD order) | seen D8 | `PK\\x01\\x02` walk, name @+46 | `zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(b)).namelist()` | high (carry-over) |\n36\t| 9 | `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` | seen D9 | `MZ`, e_lfanew @0x3C, `PE\\0\\0` | `pefile.PE(data=b).FILE_HEADER.Machine` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n37\t| 10 | `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` | seen D10 | opt hdr +16 | `pe.OPTIONAL_HEADER.AddressOfEntryPoint` 