d sizes/hashes, declared type vs magic | gap (email-mime-attachments) | `multipart/*`, `Content-Disposition: attachment`, base64 parts | `msg.walk()`, `part.get_payload(decode=True)`, `hashlib` | high |\n115\t| 88 | E-mail auth: Authentication-Results spf/dkim/dmarc, ARC count, DKIM h=, Reply-To / Return-Path vs From domain mismatch | gap (email-auth-results) | `Authentication-Results:`, `ARC-Seal:`, `DKIM-Signature:` | regex over unfolded headers | med |\n116\t| 89 | MBOX / mailbox export: message count, Message-IDs in order, duplicates, thread groups | gap (mbox-collection) | `From ` line at 0 + RFC 5322 headers; zip of many `.eml` | split on `^From ` (unescape `>From`), `email.message_from_bytes` per message | med-high |\n117\t| 90 | iCalendar / vCard: UID, ORGANIZER, ATTENDEE, DTSTART, SUMMARY; FN, EMAIL, TEL, ORG | gap (ics-vcard) | `BEGIN:VCALENDAR` / `BEGIN:VCARD` | RFC 5545/6350 line unfolding + `KEY;PARAM=..:value` split | low-med (mail attachment) |\n118\t| 91 | `.library-ms` / `.searchConnector-ms` / `.url` phishing shortcuts | gap (url-library-ms) | XML `libraryDescription` ns / `[InternetShortcut]` | `xml.etree` local-name; configparser | low-med |\n119\t| 92 | TNEF `winmail.dat`: attachment names, message class | gap (tnef-winmail) | `78 9f 3e 22` @0 | struct attribute walk | low |\n120\t\n121\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n122\t\n123\t```\n124\t4d 5a (MZ) .. \"PE\\0\\0\"@e_lfanew   PE      pefile.PE(data=b): FILE_HEADER / OPTIONAL_HEADER / DIRECTORY_ENTRY_{DEBUG,IMPORT,RESOURCE,SECURITY}\n125\t  + data dir 14 / \"BSJB\"          .NET    lib.meta.dotnet / dnfile.dnPE(data=b).net\n126\t  + data dir 4 non-zero           signed  lief.parse(b).signatures ; data dir 4 VirtualAddress is a FILE OFFSET\n127\t  + \"RSDS\"                        PDB     pe.DIRECTORY_ENTRY_DEBUG[i].entry.PdbFileName\n128\t  + \"Rich\" before PE              rich    pe.parse_rich_header(), pe.get_rich_header_hash()\n129\t7f 45 4c 46                       ELF     elftools ELFFile(io.BytesIO(b)); readelf -hn\n130\tcf fa ed fe / ce fa ed fe / ca fe ba be  Mach-O / fat   struct; rabin2 -I; lief\n131\td0 cf 11 e0 a1 b1 1a e1           CFB     olefile.OleFileIO(b).listdir() then route by streams:\n132\t  !_StringPool + !Property          MSI     lib.meta.msi ; msiinfo (tools/msitools/usr/bin)\n133\t  WordDocument/Workbook/PowerPoint  Office  ole.get_metadata(); olevba (Macros/_VBA_PROJECT)\n134\t  DestList + hex streams            JumpList AppID = filename; streams = LNK\n135\t  __substg1.0_*                     MSG     subject 0037001F, headers 007D001F, msg-id 1035001F; Catalog = Thumbs.db\n136\t50 4b 03 04 (PK)                  ZIP     zipfile; then route by member names:\n137\t  [Content_Types].xml               OOXML   rels / docProps core,app,custom / settings.xml.rels template\n138\t  AppxManifest.xml                  MSIX    Identity Name/Publisher/Version\n139\t  META-INF/MANIFEST.MF / classes.dex  JAR/APK (mobile lane)\n140\t  mimetype=application/epub+zip     EPUB    META-INF/container.xml -> OPF dc:*\n141\t4c 00 00 00 01 14 02 00           LNK     lib.meta.lnk / LnkParse3; LinkInfo vs IDList may disagree\n142\t[InternetShortcut]                .url    URL= line\n143\t45 6c 66 46 69 6c 65 00 (ElfFile) EVTX    Evtx FileHeader(b,0).chunks() -> records -> rec.xml()\n144\t72 65 67 66 (regf)                Hive    struct base block; regipy (needs path) for keys/values\n145\t.. .. .. .. 53 43 43 41 (SCCA@4)  Prefetch v17/23/26/30; \"MAM\\x04\"@0 = Win10 compressed (LZXpress Huffman)\n146\t01/02 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 + size $I      RecycleBin: size@8, FILETIME@16, path@24 (v1) / len@24 path@28 (v2)\n147\t46 49 4c 45 (FILE0)               $MFT    1024-B records; attr 0x10 $SI, 0x30 $FN (compare -> timestomp)\n148\tff fe 3c 00 3f 00 78 00 (<?x)     UTF-16 XML: `<Task` + mit/task ns = TaskXML -> Actions/Exec/Command\n149\tff fe 57 00 69 00 6e 00 (Win)     .reg    \"Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00\"\n150\t4d 53 43 46 (MSCF)                CAB     CFHEADER; 7z l -slt\n151\t25 50 44 46 2d (%PDF-)            PDF     header ver @5; trailer /Info; count %%EOF; pdfinfo / qpdf --json / pdfid\n152\t7b 5c 72 74 66 ({\\rtf)            RTF     rtfobj (oletools) for \\objdata\n153\te4 52 5c 7b 8c d8 a7 4d           OneNote carve FileDataStoreObject\n154\tff d8 ff                          JPEG    SOF dims; APP1 Exif -> PIL getexif()/get_ifd(0x8825) or exiftool -j -n\n155\t89 50 4e 47 0d 0a 1a 0a           PNG     IHDR@16; chunk walk tEXt/iTXt/zTXt/tIME; bytes after IEND\n156\t47 49 46 38 37/39 61              GIF     w,h u16LE @6/@8; 21 fe comment\n157\t42 4d (BM) / 00 00 01 00          BMP/ICO DIB w,h @18/@22 (i32) / count u16 @4\n158\t.. .. .. .. 66 74 79 70 (ftyp@4)  MP4/MOV box walk -> moov/mvhd creation_time (secs since 1904-01-01)\n159\t49 44 33 (ID3) / \"TAG\"@-128       MP3     ID3v2 frames TIT2/TPE1/COMM\n160\t52 49 46 46 .. 57 41 56 45        WAV     fmt (rate@24, ch@22), LIST/INFO\n161\t66 4c 61 43 (fLaC)                FLAC    STREAMINFO, block 4 VORBIS_COMMENT\n162\t1f 8b 08                          GZIP    FNAME if flg&8, MTIME u32LE@4, OS@9, ISIZE = last 4\n163\t\"ustar\" @257                      TAR     tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b))\n164\t37 7a bc af 27 1c                 7z      major/minor @6/@7; 7z l -slt\n165\t52 61 72 21 1a 07 00 / 01 00      RAR4/5\n166\t\"CD001\" @0x8001                   ISO     PVD @0x8000: system id @+8, volume id @+40, creation date @+813\n167\t\"conectix\" last 512 / vhdxfile / KDMV / QFI\\xfb  VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2   qemu-img info --output=json\n168\t53 51 4c 69 74 65 20 66 6f 72 6d 61 74 20 33 00  SQLite page size u16BE@16; sqlite3 .deserialize(b)\n169\td4 c3 b2 a1 / a1 b2 c3 d4 / 0a 0d 0d 0a  PCAP/PCAPNG  linktype u32 @20; capinfos -M; dpkt\n170\t-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE----- / 30 82 ..  X.509   cryptography x509 load_*; openssl x509 -noout -text -fingerprint -sha256\n171\tReceived: / Message-ID: / MIME-Version:  EML (GM fmt `email`)  lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(b, {\"field\": f}); values VERBATIM\n172\t  (Message-ID keeps <>); first hop = LAST Received; threads: References[0] / In-Reply-To; parts: msg.walk()\n173\t\"From \" @0 + headers               MBOX    split on ^From , unescape >From, parse each message\n174\tBEGIN:VCALENDAR / BEGIN:VCARD      ICS/VCF unfold CRLF+space, KEY;PARAM:value\n175\tef bb bf / ff fe / fe ff          BOM     text.*_bom_present\n176\tTime fields: FILETIME = 100ns since 1601 (/1e7 - 11644473600); WebKit = us since 1601; PRTime = us since 1970;\n177\t  Mac/MP4 = s since 1904; DOS date/time = 2-s resolution, local. Spelling unverified -> prefer ISO-8601 `Z` for `_utc`.\n178\tHex fields: `0x` + lowercase, zero-padded to the STRUCT width (`_u16_hex` 4 digits, `_u32_hex` 8). GUIDs follow source.\n179\t```\n180\t\n181\t## Readiness gaps\n182\t\n183\tRanking: priority 1 = plausible D17-D19 question with no extractor, or a harness blocker that silently fails a\n184\twhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\n185\t\n186\t```json\n187\t[\n188\t  {\"id\": \"email-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `email` -> prebuilt `eml` fields\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/email.py re-registering EVERY ('eml', f) field of lib/meta/prebuilt/eml.py under fmt 'email' (also 'mail', 'mime') with the same extractor. D16 GM asked email.message_id; the eml-registered extractor was invisible to the solver. Message-ID verbatim WITH angle brackets (GM-verified D16).\"},\n189\t  {\"id\": \"email-threading\", \"concept\": \"In-Reply-To / References / thread root / reply-forward flags\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml alias), fields in_reply_to, references (compact JSON list, stored order, each id with <>), references_count, thread_root_message_id (References[0] else In-Reply-To else own Message-ID), parent_message_id (last References id else In-Reply-To), is_reply, is_forward (Re:/Fwd:/FW: prefix or X-Forwarded-*), normalized_subject (strip Re:/Fwd: repeatedly), thread_index_guid (Outlook Thread-Index base64: 22-byte header = FILETIME-ish 6 B + GUID 16 B), thread_topic, resent_message_id, header_<name> generic (first occurrence, unfolded, verbatim). stdlib email only.\"},\n190\t  {\"id\": \"email-mime-attachments\", \"concept\": \"MIME tree, attachment names/sizes/hashes/types\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email, fields mime_part_count, content_type (top-level, no params), mime_boundary, attachment_count, attachment_names (MIME order), attachment_content_types, attachment_sizes_bytes (decoded), attachment_sha256s / md5s / sha1s (decoded payload), attachment_magic_prefix_hex_16, attachment_declared_vs_magic_mismatch, body_text_sha256, content_transfer_encodings. msg.walk() + get_payload(decode=True); RFC 2231/2047 filenames decoded.\"},\n191\t  {\"id\": \"mbox-collection\", \"concept\": \"MBOX / mailbox export: count, ids, duplicates, threads\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mbox (alias mailbox), fields message_count, message_ids (file order, with <>), unique_message_id_count, duplicate_message_ids (sorted), thread_count, thread_root_ids, subjects, first_date_utc, last_date_utc. Split bytes on b'\\\\nFrom ' (first line at 0), unescape '>From ', parse each with email.message_from_bytes (stdlib mailbox needs a path -> not allowed).\"},\n192\t  {\"id\": \"email-thread-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-message threading over several .eml members\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 flavor: 'rebuild which mail actually belongs together'. Add to lib.meta.synthesis: thread_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` list -> group by thread root (References/In-Reply-To, union-find), dedupe by Message-ID, order members by Date then filename; outputs: compact JSON array of arrays (filenames), thread_count, duplicate filenames, root filename per thread. Spelling unverified -> register sorted-filename variant and keep date order as an alternate.\"},\n193\t  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"},\n194\t  {\"id\": \"pe-debug-rich-imports\", \"concept\": \"PE PDB path / Rich header / imphash / imports / exports / Authenticode\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Re-run the REJECTED target without `import ordlookup` (pefile.PE.get_imphash already handles ordinals). fmt pe, fields debug_pdb_path, debug_codeview_guid, debug_codeview_age, rich_header_hash_md5, rich_header_xor_key_u32_hex, imphash, import_dll_names, export_names, export_dll_name. Do not re-register time_date_stamp_u32_hex (exists).\"},\n195\t  {\"id\": \"pe-authenticode\", \"concept\": \"PE Authenticode signer / cert serial / thumbprint / signing time\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pe, fields is_signed, security_dir_size_u32_hex, signer_subject_cn, signer_issuer_cn, signer_serial_hex, signer_cert_sha1, signer_cert_sha256, signing_time_utc. Data dir 4 VirtualAddress is a file offset; WIN_CERTIFICATE (len u32, rev 0x0200, type 2) + PKCS#7 SignedData. Needs asn1crypto/cryptography in ALLOWED_IMPORTS or a minimal stdlib DER walker.\"},\n196\t  {\"id\": \"evtx-records\", \"concept\": \"EVTX record fields (EventID, TimeCreated, Provider, Channel, Computer, count)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt evtx: record_count, first_event_id, first_time_created_utc, provider_names, channel, computer_name) + event_ids (ordered list), last_event_record_id, event_data_<name> family. Blocked by gate-allowlist-dfir-libs unless a stdlib BinXML walker is written (template substitution makes that ~400 lines; widening the allowlist for Evtx is cheaper).\"},\n197\t  {\"id\": \"regf-values\", \"concept\": \"Registry key/value lookups (Run keys, last-write, counts, UserAssist)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt regf: run_key_values, last_written_utc, subkey_count, value_count, userassist_entries) + value_<path> family, computer_name, timezone_key_name. Use a struct nk/vk/lf/lh/ri walker over hbins (stdlib) since regipy needs a file path and is not allowlisted.\"},\n198\t  {\"id\": \"recycle-bin-i\", \"concept\": \"Recycle Bin $I original path / deletion time / size\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Split from target jumplist-recycle-mft so it lands alone: fmt recycle (also alias fmt recyclebin), fields original_path, deleted_time_utc, original_size, format_version. v1: header=1, size u64@8, FILETIME@16, UTF-16 path 520 B@24; v2: header=2, path chars u32@24, path@28. Pure struct, ~40 lines.\"},\n199\t  {\"id\": \"prefetch\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch exe name / run count / last run times / volume info\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt prefetch: executable_name, run_count, last_run_time_utc, format_version, prefetch_hash_u32_hex, volume_serial_u32_hex) + last_run_times_utc (list of 8), volume_device_path, referenced_file_count. Uncompressed SCCA v17/23/26/30 is struct-only; Win10 MAM\\\\x04 needs an LZXpress-Huffman decoder (stdlib port ~120 lines, or tool dissect.util).\"},\n200\t  {\"id\": \"task-xml\", \"concept\": \"Scheduled task XML (Command, Arguments, Author, Date, URI, Triggers)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt task (aliases scheduled_task, task_xml), fields exec_command, exec_arguments, registration_author, registration_date, uri, principal_user_id, run_level, trigger_types, hidden. UTF-16LE BOM XML, ns http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task; xml.etree with local-name matching.\"},\n201\t  {\"id\": \"ole-vba\", \"concept\": \"VBA macro project (module names, auto-exec, stomping)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt vba (and ole alias fields), fields module_names, project_name, has_macros, autoexec_keywords, vba_stream_names, code_page. Reuse lib/meta/cfb.py cfb_streams; dir stream is MS-OVBA RLE-compressed (port the ~40-line decompressor, stdlib). Covers .doc/.xls CFB and OOXML word/vbaProject.bin.\"},\n202\t  {\"id\": \"ooxml-siblings\", \"concept\": \"OOXML custom props / remote template / embeddings / internal rel targets\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt ooxml, fields custom_properties (JSON name->value), attached_template_target, internal_relationship_targets, relationship_types, embedded_object_names, has_vba_project, main_part_content_type, hyperlink_count. Mirror D15 conventions (compact JSON, sorted for gathered sets). external_relationship_targets is verified -- do not re-register.\"},\n203\t  {\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) now exists (D15 sha256 order, re-asked D16 as metadata-day-16-synthesis-sha256-order with today's new member in Files). D16 both timed modes went solver_incomplete because the day's solver template did not call it -- the template/shared dispatch must route every `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-*` id to lib.meta.synthesis. Still to add there: md5/sha1/size order, duplicate groups, earliest/latest by embedded timestamp, email thread grouping (see email-thread-synthesis).\"},\n204\t  {\"id\": \"email-auth-results\", \"concept\": \"SPF/DKIM/DMARC results, ARC, sender mismatch\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email, fields spf_result, dkim_result, dmarc_result, authserv_id, arc_seal_count, dkim_signed_headers (h= list), return_path_domain, from_domain, reply_to_domain, from_return_path_mismatch, reply_to_mismatch, received_spf_result. Regex over unfolded Authentication-Results / Received-SPF / DKIM-Signature.\"},\n205\t  {\"id\": \"outlook-msg\", \"concept\": \"Outlook .msg (CFB) message properties\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt msg (alias outlook_msg), fields message_id (__substg1.0_1035001F), in_reply_to (1042001F), subject (0037001F), sender_email (0C1F001F/5D01001F), message_class (001A001F), transport_headers (007D001F), attachment_names (__attach_version1.0_#*/3707001F else 3704001F), attachment_count, client_submit_time_utc (__properties_version1.0 0x00390040 FILETIME). Reuse lib/meta/cfb.py streams; UTF-16LE for 001F.\"},\n206\t  {\"id\": \"ics-vcard\", \"concept\": \"iCalendar / vCard fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt ics (aliases ical, calendar): uid, organizer, attendees, dtstart_utc, dtend_utc, summary, location, method, prodid, event_count; fmt vcard (alias vcf): fn, email, tel, org, uid, version. RFC 5545 unfolding (CRLF + space/tab), parameters split on ';', value after first ':'.\"},\n207\t  {\"id\": \"url-library-ms\", \"concept\": \"`.url` / `.library-ms` / `.searchConnector-ms` shortcuts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt url (alias internet_shortcut): url, icon_file, icon_index, working_directory, hotkey; fmt library_ms (aliases library, searchconnector): location_urls (simpleLocation/url), is_library_pinned, folder_type, owner_sid, version. configparser-free line parse; xml.etree local names.\"},\n208\t  {\"id\": \"jumplist\", \"concept\": \"Jump list AutomaticDestinations AppID + DestList + embedded LNK targets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt jumplist, fields app_id (from member filename), destlist_entry_count, destlist_paths, lnk_stream_names, first_target_path. cfb_streams + reuse prebuilt lnk parser on each numeric stream. DestList v3/v4 entry layout struct.\"},\n209\t  {\"id\": \"pdf-info\", \"concept\": \"PDF Info dict / page count / %%EOF count / Encrypt / JS\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt pdf: info_title ... encrypted) + has_javascript, open_action_present, embedded_file_names, xmp_creator_tool. Handle /ObjStm via zlib. pdf.header_version is verified -- don't touch.\"},\n210\t  {\"id\": \"exif\", \"concept\": \"JPEG EXIF Make/Model/DateTimeOriginal/GPS\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt jpeg: exif_make ... app_segments) + exif_software, exif_gps_longitude, exif_gps_decimal, xmp_creator_tool. Pure-Python TIFF IFD walker (II/MM), GPS rationals -> decimal degrees; spelling unknown -> also store DMS.\"},\n211\t  {\"id\": \"png-text-time\", \"concept\": \"PNG tEXt/iTXt/zTXt/tIME, chunk order, trailing data\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt png: text_chunks, time_chunk, chunk_names, ihdr_bit_depth, ihdr_color_type) + trailing_bytes_after_iend, text_<keyword> family.\"},\n212\t  {\"id\": \"mft-record\", \"concept\": \"$MFT FILE record $SI vs $FN timestamps, name, parent\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mft, fields file_name, record_number, parent_record_number, si_created_utc, si_modified_utc, fn_created_utc, fn_modified_utc, timestomp_suspected, is_directory, resident_data_hex_16. Apply update-sequence fixups first.\"},\n213\t  {\"id\": \"elf-header\", \"concept\": \"ELF header / PT_INTERP / build-id / sections\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt elf); pyelftools is allowlisted. Don't re-register e_machine_u16_hex / e_entry_hex / entry_point_hex.\"},\n214\t  {\"id\": \"archives\", \"concept\": \"GZIP/TAR/7z/RAR/ISO headers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt gzip) + separate modules tar (member_names, ustar_magic, member_mtimes_utc, member_unames), 7z (signature_version, next_header_offset), rar (version), iso (primary_volume_id, system_id, volume_creation_date, publisher_id). Headers only.\"},\n215\t  {\"id\": \"x509-cert\", \"concept\": \"X.509 subject/issuer/serial/validity/fingerprint\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt x509 (alias cert), fields subject_cn, issuer_cn, serial_hex, not_before_utc, not_after_utc, sha256_fingerprint, sha1_fingerprint, san_dns_names. Shares the DER walker with pe-authenticode; cryptography needs the allowlist.\"},\n216\t  {\"id\": \"sqlite-header\", \"concept\": \"SQLite header + table names + browser history\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt sqlite, fields page_size, text_encoding, user_version, application_id_u32_hex, table_names, page_count. Header is pure struct; table names via sqlite_master page-1 b-tree walk (stdlib), or allowlist sqlite3 (`connect(':memory:').deserialize(b)`, Py3.12 has it).\"},\n217\t  {\"id\": \"tool-mutagen-pypdf\", \"concept\": \"Media tag + PDF python libs for the worker\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install mutagen pypdf pymediainfo exifread (all pure-Python; worker-side convenience -- exiftool already covers most fields).\"},\n218\t  {\"id\": \"tool-dfir-parsers\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch / MFT / MSG / archive libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install dissect.util (LZXpress Huffman for Win10 prefetch), python-registry, extract_msg, py7zr, rarfile, pycdlib, analyzeMFT, windowsprefetch. apt: genisoimage (isoinfo), libscca-utils (sccainfo), osslsigncode.\"},\n219\t  {\"id\": \"tnef-winmail\", \"concept\": \"TNEF winmail.dat attachments\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt tnef (alias winmail): signature_u32_hex (0x223e9f78), key_u16, message_class, attachment_names (attAttachTitle 0x00018010), attachment_count, attachment_sizes_bytes. Level/attr id/len/data/checksum walk.\"},\n220\t  {\"id\": \"pcap-header\", \"concept\": \"PCAP/PCAPNG global header, linktype, packet count, interfaces\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pcap / pcapng, fields magic_u32_hex, version, linktype, snaplen, packet_count, first_packet_time_utc, if_names (pcapng IDB if_name option 2), shb_os. Pure struct.\"},\n221\t  {\"id\": \"media-tags\", \"concept\": \"MP4 mvhd / ID3 / WAV INFO / FLAC Vorbis\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Modules mp4 (ftyp_major_brand, mvhd_creation_time_utc, duration_seconds), mp3 (id3_title, id3_artist, id3_comment, id3_version), wav (fmt_sample_rate, fmt_channels, info_<tag>), flac (streaminfo_sample_rate, vorbis_<tag>). Pure struct.\"},\n222\t  {\"id\": \"macho-header\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O cputype/filetype/ncmds/LC_UUID\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt macho).\"},\n223\t  {\"id\": \"rtf-onenote\", \"concept\": \"RTF \\\\objdata OLE1 objects, OneNote embedded files\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt rtf: object_class_names, object_count, template_target, info_author; fmt onenote: embedded_file_count, embedded_file_sha256s. Hex-decode \\\\objdata, OLE1 header (class name len-prefixed).\"},\n224\t  {\"id\": \"msitools-path\", \"concept\": \"msitools present but not on PATH\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"tools/msitools/usr/bin/{msiinfo,msidump,msiextract,gcab} exist but `source bin/env.sh` doesn't expose them; add a bin/ shim. reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md still says 'Not installed: msitools, LnkParse3, dnfile' -- all three are now present (LnkParse3 + dnfile in .venv).\"}\n225\t]\n226\t```\n227\tmetadata-forensics:archives True 1\n228\tmetadata-forensics:cab True 1\n229\tmetadata-forensics:dotnet-assembly True 1\n230\tmetadata-forensics:elf-header True 1\n231\tmetadata-forensics:email-auth-results True 1\n232\tmetadata-forensics:email-fmt-alias True 1\n233\tmetadata-forensics:email-mime-attachments True 1\n234\tmetadata-forensics:email-thread-synthesis True 1\n235\tmetadata-forensics:email-threading True 1\n236\tmetadata-forensics:eml-headers True 1\n237\tmetadata-forensics:evtx True 1\n238\tmetadata-forensics:evtx-records True 2\n239\tmetadata-forensics:exif True 1\n240\tmetadata-forensics:gif-bmp-ico-wav True 1\n241\tmetadata-forensics:ics-vcard False 1\n242\tmetadata-forensics:jumplist True 1\n243\tmetadata-forensics:lnk True 1\n244\tmetadata-forensics:lnk-linkinfo True 1\n245\tmetadata-forensics:macho-header True 1\n246\tmetadata-forensics:mbox-collection True 1\n247\tmetadata-forensics:media-tags True 1\n248\tmetadata-forensics:mft-record True 1\n249\tmetadata-forensics:msi-siblings True 2\n250\tmetadata-forensics:ole-summary True 1\n251\tmetadata-forensics:ole-vba True 1\n252\tmetadata-forensics:ooxml-docprops True 1\n253\tmetadata-forensics:ooxml-siblings True 1\n254\tmetadata-forensics:outlook-msg True 1\n255\tmetadata-forensics:pcap-header True 1\n256\tmetadata-forensics:pdf-info True 1\n257\tmetadata-forensics:pe-authenticode True 1\n258\tmetadata-forensics:pe-debug-rich-imports True 2\n259\tmetadata-forensics:pe-header-fields True 1\n260\tmetadata-forensics:pe-version-keys True 1\n261\tmetadata-forensics:png-text-time True 1\n262\tmetadata-forensics:prefetch True 1\n263\tmetadata-forensics:recycle-bin-i True 1\n264\tmetadata-forensics:regf True 1\n265\tmetadata-forensics:regf-values True 1\n266\tmetadata-forensics:rtf-onenote True 1\n267\tmetadata-forensics:sqlite-header True 1\n268\tmetadata-forensics:task-xml True 1\n269\tmetadata-forensics:tnef-winmail True 1\n270\tmetadata-forensics:url-library-ms False 1\n271\tmetadata-forensics:x509-cert True 1\n272\tmetadata-forensics:zip-members True 1\n273\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1bd2628-a8d7-4c8d-ac28-4d4570a86f8b","uuid":"b943bd74-c405-4ca6-a142-21e233bbabd3","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:10:40.513Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/d1bd2628-a8d7-4c8d-ac28-4d4570a86f8b/tool-results/b2qt4773z.txt","content":"# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D16, 2026-10-16)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:82`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\noletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\nworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n**Likelihood** reasoning: D9-D15 walked Windows binaries/installers/shortcuts/Office (PE -> PE version -> .NET -> MSI\n-> LNK -> OOXML); the next steps are most plausibly other Windows DFIR artifacts and legacy-Office/CFB siblings,\nplus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 added cross-file synthesis).\n**D16 turned to e-mail** (`email.message_id` of one `.eml`; flavor \"replies, forwards, duplicates, reconstructed\nmessages ... stable message identities\"). PE stayed three days (D9-11) with a deeper field each day, so D17-D19 most\nplausibly ask deeper `email.*` fields (In-Reply-To / References / attachments / Received / auth) or a sibling mail\ncontainer (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis question. GM fmt word is `email`, not `eml`.\n\n## 1. Atlas\n\n| # | Concept / field | Status | Recognition cues | Standard tool / lib + exact call | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Identity: filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | seen D1 (+D15 member roster) | any member; id stem names WHICH member | `hashlib.<algo>(b).hexdigest()`; `sha256sum` (I) | high -- every timed kit |\n| 2 | `file.magic_prefix_hex_N` | seen D2 | first N bytes | `xxd -p -l 16` (I); `b[:N].hex()` | high (carry-over) |\n| 3 | `text.utf8_bom_present` (utf16 sibling speculative) | seen D3 | `ef bb bf` / `ff fe` / `fe ff` | `b.startswith(codecs.BOM_UTF8)` | high (carry-over) |\n| 4 | `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` | seen D4 | `ff d8 ff`; SOFn `ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc | segment walk; `identify -format %wx%h` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 5 | `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` | seen D5 | `89 50 4e 47 0d 0a 1a 0a`; IHDR @12 | `struct.unpack('>II', b[16:24])`; `pngcheck -v` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 6 | `pdf.header_version` | seen D6 | `%PDF-x.y` @0 | `b[5:8]`; `pdfinfo` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 7 | `zip.eocd_total_entries` | seen D7 | `PK\\x05\\x06` last; u16 @+10 | struct; `7z l -slt` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 8 | `zip.central_directory_member_names` (CD order) | seen D8 | `PK\\x01\\x02` walk, name @+46 | `zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(b)).namelist()` | high (carry-over) |\n| 9 | `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` | seen D9 | `MZ`, e_lfanew @0x3C, `PE\\0\\0` | `pefile.PE(data=b).FILE_HEADER.Machine` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 10 | `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` | seen D10 | opt hdr +16 | `pe.OPTIONAL_HEADER.AddressOfEntryPoint` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 11 | `pe.version_original_filename` (+ `pe.version_*` family) | seen D11 | RT_VERSION, `VS_VERSION_INFO` UTF-16 | `pe.FileInfo[..].StringTable[0].entries` (I); `exiftool -j` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 12 | `dotnet.mvid_guid` | seen D12 | data dir 14 -> `BSJB` -> `#GUID` | `lib.meta.dotnet`; `dnfile.dnPE(data=b)` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 13 | `msi.product_code_guid` (+ Property siblings speculative) | seen D13 | `d0 cf 11 e0 a1 b1 1a e1` + `!_StringPool` | `lib.meta.msi`; `tools/msitools/usr/bin/msiinfo export x.msi Property` (I, not on PATH) | high (carry-over) |\n| 14 | `lnk.target_path_windows` | seen D14 | `4c 00 00 00` + CLSID `01 14 02 00 ...46` | `lib.meta.lnk`; `LnkParse3.lnk_file(io.BytesIO(b)).get_json()` (I) | high (carry-over) |\n| 15 | `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` (sorted) | seen D15 | `PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`; `*.rels` `TargetMode=\"External\"` | `zipfile` + `xml.etree` over every `.rels` | high (carry-over) |\n| 16 | Synthesis: `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order` | seen D15, D16 (`lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`) | id `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`, `Files: [...]` in text | day15 solver `_digest_order`; `hashlib.new(algo)` | high -- expect md5/sha1/size siblings |\n| 17 | PE COFF/optional header: TimeDateStamp, NumberOfSections, Subsystem, Characteristics, DllCharacteristics, SizeOfImage, CheckSum, section names | prebuilt pe | COFF @e_lfanew+4; opt @+24 | `pe.FILE_HEADER.TimeDateStamp`, `[s.Name.rstrip(b'\\0') for s in pe.sections]` (I) | high -- natural PE sibling |\n| 18 | PE VS_FIXEDFILEINFO file/product version, flags, OS | prebuilt pe | `bd 04 ef fe` signature in RT_VERSION | `pe.VS_FIXEDFILEINFO[0].FileVersionMS` (I) | med |\n| 19 | .NET assembly name/version/culture/PKT, module name, runtime `v4.0.30319`, TypeDef count | prebuilt dotnet | `BSJB` root, `#~` stream | `dnfile.dnPE(data=b).net.mdtables.Assembly[0]` (I); `ilspycmd` (I) | high -- .NET sibling |\n| 20 | MSI SummaryInformation: PackageCode (PID 9), Title, Author, Template `Intel;1033`, PageCount; ProductVersion/UpgradeCode | prebuilt msi | `\\x05SummaryInformation` stream in CFB | `olefile.OleFileIO(b).get_metadata()` (I); `msiinfo suminfo` (I) | med-high |\n| 21 | CAB CFHEADER folders/files/setID/cbCabinet/version, CFFILE names | prebuilt cab | `MSCF` @0 | struct; `7z l -slt x.cab` (I); `gcab -t` (I msitools) | med (MSI embeds cabs) |\n| 22 | LNK header: LinkFlags, FileAttributes, C/A/W FILETIMEs, FileSize, show cmd, hotkey, args, working dir | prebuilt lnk | header 0x4C bytes; times @0x1C/0x24/0x2C | `LnkParse3` (I); `exiftool -j` (I) | high -- LNK siblings |\n| 23 | LNK LinkInfo volume label/serial/drive type, net path, IDList path, env block, icon, TrackerDataBlock machine id/droid | prebuilt lnk | LinkInfo flags; ExtraData sigs `0xA0000001` env, `0xA0000003` tracker | `LnkParse3 ... ['link_info']`, `['extra']` (I) | high |\n| 24 | Windows `.url` InternetShortcut `URL=` / `IconFile=` | gap | text `[InternetShortcut]` | `configparser` / regex | med (shortcut sibling) |\n| 25 | EVTX file header: chunk count, next record id, first record id, version | prebuilt evtx | `ElfFile\\0` @0; `ElfChnk\\0` @0x1000 | struct; `evtx_info` (I) | high |\n| 26 | EVTX records: count, EventID, TimeCreated, Provider, Channel, Computer, EventRecordID | prebuilt evtx | record magic `2a 2a 00 00`; BinXML | `Evtx.Evtx.FileHeader(b,0).chunks()` -> `rec.xml()` (I, worker-only); `evtx_dump.py` (I) | high -- top DFIR artifact |\n| 27 | EVTX semantic: 4624 LogonType/TargetUserName/IpAddress, 4688 NewProcessName/CommandLine, 7045 ServiceName/ImagePath, 4104 ScriptBlockText, 1102 clear | gap | `<EventID>4624</EventID>` in record XML | as #26 + `xml.etree` on `rec.xml()`; `evtx_filter_records` (I) | med-high |\n| 28 | Registry hive base block: seq numbers, last written, hive name, versio