bKit = us since 1601; PRTime = us since 1970;\n  Mac/MP4 = s since 1904; DOS date/time = 2-s resolution, local. Spelling unverified -> prefer ISO-8601 `Z` for `_utc`.\nHex fields: `0x` + lowercase, zero-padded to the STRUCT width (`_u16_hex` 4 digits, `_u32_hex` 8). GUIDs follow source.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking: priority 1 = plausible D17-D19 question with no extractor, or a harness blocker that silently fails a\nwhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"email-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `email` -> prebuilt `eml` fields\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/email.py re-registering EVERY ('eml', f) field of lib/meta/prebuilt/eml.py under fmt 'email' (also 'mail', 'mime') with the same extractor. D16 GM asked email.message_id; the eml-registered extractor was invisible to the solver. Message-ID verbatim WITH angle brackets (GM-verified D16).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-threading\", \"concept\": \"In-Reply-To / References / thread root / reply-forward flags\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml alias), fields in_reply_to, references (compact JSON list, stored order, each id with <>), references_count, thread_root_message_id (References[0] else In-Reply-To else own Message-ID), parent_message_id (last References id else In-Reply-To), is_reply, is_forward (Re:/Fwd:/FW: prefix or X-Forwarded-*), normalized_subject (strip Re:/Fwd: repeatedly), thread_index_guid (Outlook Thread-Index base64: 22-byte header = FILETIME-ish 6 B + GUID 16 B), thread_topic, resent_message_id, header_<name> generic (first occurrence, unfolded, verbatim). stdlib email only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-mime-attachments\", \"concept\": \"MIME tree, attachment names/sizes/hashes/types\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email, fields mime_part_count, content_type (top-level, no params), mime_boundary, attachment_count, attachment_names (MIME order), attachment_content_types, attachment_sizes_bytes (decoded), attachment_sha256s / md5s / sha1s (decoded payload), attachment_magic_prefix_hex_16, attachment_declared_vs_magic_mismatch, body_text_sha256, content_transfer_encodings. msg.walk() + get_payload(decode=True); RFC 2231/2047 filenames decoded.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mbox-collection\", \"concept\": \"MBOX / mailbox export: count, ids, duplicates, threads\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mbox (alias mailbox), fields message_count, message_ids (file order, with <>), unique_message_id_count, duplicate_message_ids (sorted), thread_count, thread_root_ids, subjects, first_date_utc, last_date_utc. Split bytes on b'\\\\nFrom ' (first line at 0), unescape '>From ', parse each with email.message_from_bytes (stdlib mailbox needs a path -> not allowed).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-thread-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-message threading over several .eml members\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 flavor: 'rebuild which mail actually belongs together'. Add to lib.meta.synthesis: thread_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` list -> group by thread root (References/In-Reply-To, union-find), dedupe by Message-ID, order members by Date then filename; outputs: compact JSON array of arrays (filenames), thread_count, duplicate filenames, root filename per thread. Spelling unverified -> register sorted-filename variant and keep date order as an alternate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pe-debug-rich-imports\", \"concept\": \"PE PDB path / Rich header / imphash / imports / exports / Authenticode\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Re-run the REJECTED target without `import ordlookup` (pefile.PE.get_imphash already handles ordinals). fmt pe, fields debug_pdb_path, debug_codeview_guid, debug_codeview_age, rich_header_hash_md5, rich_header_xor_key_u32_hex, imphash, import_dll_names, export_names, export_dll_name. Do not re-register time_date_stamp_u32_hex (exists).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pe-authenticode\", \"concept\": \"PE Authenticode signer / cert serial / thumbprint / signing time\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pe, fields is_signed, security_dir_size_u32_hex, signer_subject_cn, signer_issuer_cn, signer_serial_hex, signer_cert_sha1, signer_cert_sha256, signing_time_utc. Data dir 4 VirtualAddress is a file offset; WIN_CERTIFICATE (len u32, rev 0x0200, type 2) + PKCS#7 SignedData. Needs asn1crypto/cryptography in ALLOWED_IMPORTS or a minimal stdlib DER walker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"evtx-records\", \"concept\": \"EVTX record fields (EventID, TimeCreated, Provider, Channel, Computer, count)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt evtx: record_count, first_event_id, first_time_created_utc, provider_names, channel, computer_name) + event_ids (ordered list), last_event_record_id, event_data_<name> family. Blocked by gate-allowlist-dfir-libs unless a stdlib BinXML walker is written (template substitution makes that ~400 lines; widening the allowlist for Evtx is cheaper).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"regf-values\", \"concept\": \"Registry key/value lookups (Run keys, last-write, counts, UserAssist)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt regf: run_key_values, last_written_utc, subkey_count, value_count, userassist_entries) + value_<path> family, computer_name, timezone_key_name. Use a struct nk/vk/lf/lh/ri walker over hbins (stdlib) since regipy needs a file path and is not allowlisted.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recycle-bin-i\", \"concept\": \"Recycle Bin $I original path / deletion time / size\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Split from target jumplist-recycle-mft so it lands alone: fmt recycle (also alias fmt recyclebin), fields original_path, deleted_time_utc, original_size, format_version. v1: header=1, size u64@8, FILETIME@16, UTF-16 path 520 B@24; v2: header=2, path chars u32@24, path@28. Pure struct, ~40 lines.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prefetch\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch exe name / run count / last run times / volume info\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt prefetch: executable_name, run_count, last_run_time_utc, format_version, prefetch_hash_u32_hex, volume_serial_u32_hex) + last_run_times_utc (list of 8), volume_device_path, referenced_file_count. Uncompressed SCCA v17/23/26/30 is struct-only; Win10 MAM\\\\x04 needs an LZXpress-Huffman decoder (stdlib port ~120 lines, or tool dissect.util).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"task-xml\", \"concept\": \"Scheduled task XML (Command, Arguments, Author, Date, URI, Triggers)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt task (aliases scheduled_task, task_xml), fields exec_command, exec_arguments, registration_author, registration_date, uri, principal_user_id, run_level, trigger_types, hidden. UTF-16LE BOM XML, ns http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task; xml.etree with local-name matching.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ole-vba\", \"concept\": \"VBA macro project (module names, auto-exec, stomping)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt vba (and ole alias fields), fields module_names, project_name, has_macros, autoexec_keywords, vba_stream_names, code_page. Reuse lib/meta/cfb.py cfb_streams; dir stream is MS-OVBA RLE-compressed (port the ~40-line decompressor, stdlib). Covers .doc/.xls CFB and OOXML word/vbaProject.bin.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ooxml-siblings\", \"concept\": \"OOXML custom props / remote template / embeddings / internal rel targets\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt ooxml, fields custom_properties (JSON name->value), attached_template_target, internal_relationship_targets, relationship_types, embedded_object_names, has_vba_project, main_part_content_type, hyperlink_count. Mirror D15 conventions (compact JSON, sorted for gathered sets). external_relationship_targets is verified -- do not re-register.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) now exists (D15 sha256 order, re-asked D16 as metadata-day-16-synthesis-sha256-order with today's new member in Files). D16 both timed modes went solver_incomplete because the day's solver template did not call it -- the template/shared dispatch must route every `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-*` id to lib.meta.synthesis. Still to add there: md5/sha1/size order, duplicate groups, earliest/latest by embedded timestamp, email thread grouping (see email-thread-synthesis).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-auth-results\", \"concept\": \"SPF/DKIM/DMARC results, ARC, sender mismatch\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email, fields spf_result, dkim_result, dmarc_result, authserv_id, arc_seal_count, dkim_signed_headers (h= list), return_path_domain, from_domain, reply_to_domain, from_return_path_mismatch, reply_to_mismatch, received_spf_result. Regex over unfolded Authentication-Results / Received-SPF / DKIM-Signature.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"outlook-msg\", \"concept\": \"Outlook .msg (CFB) message properties\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt msg (alias outlook_msg), fields message_id (__substg1.0_1035001F), in_reply_to (1042001F), subject (0037001F), sender_email (0C1F001F/5D01001F), message_class (001A001F), transport_headers (007D001F), attachment_names (__attach_version1.0_#*/3707001F else 3704001F), attachment_count, client_submit_time_utc (__properties_version1.0 0x00390040 FILETIME). Reuse lib/meta/cfb.py streams; UTF-16LE for 001F.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ics-vcard\", \"concept\": \"iCalendar / vCard fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt ics (aliases ical, calendar): uid, organizer, attendees, dtstart_utc, dtend_utc, summary, location, method, prodid, event_count; fmt vcard (alias vcf): fn, email, tel, org, uid, version. RFC 5545 unfolding (CRLF + space/tab), parameters split on ';', value after first ':'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"url-library-ms\", \"concept\": \"`.url` / `.library-ms` / `.searchConnector-ms` shortcuts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt url (alias internet_shortcut): url, icon_file, icon_index, working_directory, hotkey; fmt library_ms (aliases library, searchconnector): location_urls (simpleLocation/url), is_library_pinned, folder_type, owner_sid, version. configparser-free line parse; xml.etree local names.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jumplist\", \"concept\": \"Jump list AutomaticDestinations AppID + DestList + embedded LNK targets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt jumplist, fields app_id (from member filename), destlist_entry_count, destlist_paths, lnk_stream_names, first_target_path. cfb_streams + reuse prebuilt lnk parser on each numeric stream. DestList v3/v4 entry layout struct.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pdf-info\", \"concept\": \"PDF Info dict / page count / %%EOF count / Encrypt / JS\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt pdf: info_title ... encrypted) + has_javascript, open_action_present, embedded_file_names, xmp_creator_tool. Handle /ObjStm via zlib. pdf.header_version is verified -- don't touch.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"exif\", \"concept\": \"JPEG EXIF Make/Model/DateTimeOriginal/GPS\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt jpeg: exif_make ... app_segments) + exif_software, exif_gps_longitude, exif_gps_decimal, xmp_creator_tool. Pure-Python TIFF IFD walker (II/MM), GPS rationals -> decimal degrees; spelling unknown -> also store DMS.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"png-text-time\", \"concept\": \"PNG tEXt/iTXt/zTXt/tIME, chunk order, trailing data\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt png: text_chunks, time_chunk, chunk_names, ihdr_bit_depth, ihdr_color_type) + trailing_bytes_after_iend, text_<keyword> family.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mft-record\", \"concept\": \"$MFT FILE record $SI vs $FN timestamps, name, parent\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mft, fields file_name, record_number, parent_record_number, si_created_utc, si_modified_utc, fn_created_utc, fn_modified_utc, timestomp_suspected, is_directory, resident_data_hex_16. Apply update-sequence fixups first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"elf-header\", \"concept\": \"ELF header / PT_INTERP / build-id / sections\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt elf); pyelftools is allowlisted. Don't re-register e_machine_u16_hex / e_entry_hex / entry_point_hex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"archives\", \"concept\": \"GZIP/TAR/7z/RAR/ISO headers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt gzip) + separate modules tar (member_names, ustar_magic, member_mtimes_utc, member_unames), 7z (signature_version, next_header_offset), rar (version), iso (primary_volume_id, system_id, volume_creation_date, publisher_id). Headers only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"x509-cert\", \"concept\": \"X.509 subject/issuer/serial/validity/fingerprint\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt x509 (alias cert), fields subject_cn, issuer_cn, serial_hex, not_before_utc, not_after_utc, sha256_fingerprint, sha1_fingerprint, san_dns_names. Shares the DER walker with pe-authenticode; cryptography needs the allowlist.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqlite-header\", \"concept\": \"SQLite header + table names + browser history\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt sqlite, fields page_size, text_encoding, user_version, application_id_u32_hex, table_names, page_count. Header is pure struct; table names via sqlite_master page-1 b-tree walk (stdlib), or allowlist sqlite3 (`connect(':memory:').deserialize(b)`, Py3.12 has it).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tool-mutagen-pypdf\", \"concept\": \"Media tag + PDF python libs for the worker\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install mutagen pypdf pymediainfo exifread (all pure-Python; worker-side convenience -- exiftool already covers most fields).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tool-dfir-parsers\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch / MFT / MSG / archive libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install dissect.util (LZXpress Huffman for Win10 prefetch), python-registry, extract_msg, py7zr, rarfile, pycdlib, analyzeMFT, windowsprefetch. apt: genisoimage (isoinfo), libscca-utils (sccainfo), osslsigncode.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tnef-winmail\", \"concept\": \"TNEF winmail.dat attachments\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt tnef (alias winmail): signature_u32_hex (0x223e9f78), key_u16, message_class, attachment_names (attAttachTitle 0x00018010), attachment_count, attachment_sizes_bytes. Level/attr id/len/data/checksum walk.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pcap-header\", \"concept\": \"PCAP/PCAPNG global header, linktype, packet count, interfaces\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pcap / pcapng, fields magic_u32_hex, version, linktype, snaplen, packet_count, first_packet_time_utc, if_names (pcapng IDB if_name option 2), shb_os. Pure struct.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-tags\", \"concept\": \"MP4 mvhd / ID3 / WAV INFO / FLAC Vorbis\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Modules mp4 (ftyp_major_brand, mvhd_creation_time_utc, duration_seconds), mp3 (id3_title, id3_artist, id3_comment, id3_version), wav (fmt_sample_rate, fmt_channels, info_<tag>), flac (streaminfo_sample_rate, vorbis_<tag>). Pure struct.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"macho-header\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O cputype/filetype/ncmds/LC_UUID\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt macho).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rtf-onenote\", \"concept\": \"RTF \\\\objdata OLE1 objects, OneNote embedded files\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt rtf: object_class_names, object_count, template_target, info_author; fmt onenote: embedded_file_count, embedded_file_sha256s. Hex-decode \\\\objdata, OLE1 header (class name len-prefixed).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"msitools-path\", \"concept\": \"msitools present but not on PATH\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"tools/msitools/usr/bin/{msiinfo,msidump,msiextract,gcab} exist but `source bin/env.sh` doesn't expose them; add a bin/ shim. reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md still says 'Not installed: msitools, LnkParse3, dnfile' -- all three are now present (LnkParse3 + dnfile in .venv).\"}\n]\n```\nmetadata-forensics:archives True 1\nmetadata-forensics:cab True 1\nmetadata-forensics:dotnet-assembly True 1\nmetadata-forensics:elf-header True 1\nmetadata-forensics:email-auth-results True 1\nmetadata-forensics:email-fmt-alias True 1\nmetadata-forensics:email-mime-attachments True 1\nmetadata-forensics:email-thread-synthesis True 1\nmetadata-forensics:email-threading True 1\nmetadata-forensics:eml-headers True 1\nmetadata-forensics:evtx True 1\nmetadata-forensics:evtx-records True 2\nmetadata-forensics:exif True 1\nmetadata-forensics:gif-bmp-ico-wav True 1\nmetadata-forensics:ics-vcard False 1\nmetadata-forensics:jumplist True 1\nmetadata-forensics:lnk True 1\nmetadata-forensics:lnk-linkinfo True 1\nmetadata-forensics:macho-header True 1\nmetadata-forensics:mbox-collection True 1\nmetadata-forensics:media-tags True 1\nmetadata-forensics:mft-record True 1\nmetadata-forensics:msi-siblings True 2\nmetadata-forensics:ole-summary True 1\nmetadata-forensics:ole-vba True 1\nmetadata-forensics:ooxml-docprops True 1\nmetadata-forensics:ooxml-siblings True 1\nmetadata-forensics:outlook-msg True 1\nmetadata-forensics:pcap-header True 1\nmetadata-forensics:pdf-info True 1\nmetadata-forensics:pe-authenticode True 1\nmetadata-forensics:pe-debug-rich-imports True 2\nmetadata-forensics:pe-header-fields True 1\nmetadata-forensics:pe-version-keys True 1\nmetadata-forensics:png-text-time True 1\nmetadata-forensics:prefetch True 1\nmetadata-forensics:recycle-bin-i True 1\nmetadata-forensics:regf True 1\nmetadata-forensics:regf-values True 1\nmetadata-forensics:rtf-onenote True 1\nmetadata-forensics:sqlite-header True 1\nmetadata-forensics:task-xml True 1\nmetadata-forensics:tnef-winmail True 1\nmetadata-forensics:url-library-ms False 1\nmetadata-forensics:x509-cert True 1\nmetadata-forensics:zip-members True 1\n","numLines":273,"startLine":1,"totalLines":273}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GNUns17yB34RDq8F1Decme","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
