{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg7sDLQb2NdcHCQ5UBZXz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kt6mw9era9eE8ZDwoVLoqN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"technique log (days 1-16; updated after every day)\",\"technique log (days 1-17; updated after every day)\")\nrep(\"\"\"cross-member \"synthesis\" question. **Day 16 repeated that split** (single 1 field; TT 21; Mastery 5x21 = 105, synthesis\n  again). Always pre-arm every earlier family AND yesterday's synthesis; the timed field set is not the single's.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"cross-member \"synthesis\" question. **D16 and D17 repeated that split** (single 1 field; TT 21/22; Mastery 5x21/5x22,\n  synthesis every time). Always pre-arm every earlier family AND the synthesis; the timed field set is not the single's.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"(D13) -> LNK (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> RFC 5322 `.eml` (D16, first non-Windows-binary family since D8). Each\n  new family arrives with its own `dNN` id prefix, and its fmt word is the GM's (`email`, not `eml`).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"(D13) -> LNK (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> RFC 5322 `.eml` (D16) -> RIFF/WAVE `.wav` audio (D17, first media\n  family). Each new family arrives with its own `dNN` id prefix, and its fmt word is the GM's ABSTRACT namespace, not\n  the container: `email` (not `eml`), `media` (not `wav`/`audio`) -- and the field uses ffprobe's vocabulary.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`ooxml.external_relationship_targets` -> `email.message_id`. The question literally names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`);\n  ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`); `dNN` = the member family's first day, not today.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"`ooxml.external_relationship_targets` -> `email.message_id` -> `media.primary_audio_codec_name`. The question literally\n  names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); ids read `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`);\n  `dNN` = the member family's first day, not today; `<family>` usually = `<fmt>` but NOT always (D17 `d17-audio-001-media-`).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Singles: D1-D9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13, D15 lost ONE submit to a spelling/ordering convention\n  (padding, braces, list order); D16 lost TWO (parser bug -> `none`, then stripped brackets). Every TT/Mastery since D4\n  CORRECT on its first GM submit (D15 TT and D16 TT+Mastery only after an offline generalize for the synthesis id).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Singles: D1-D9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13, D15 lost ONE submit to a spelling/ordering convention\n  (padding, braces, list order); D16 lost TWO (parser bug -> `none`, then stripped brackets); D17 first submit ~24 s.\n  Every TT/Mastery since D4 CORRECT on its first GM submit -- but D15 TT, D16 and D17 TT+Mastery only after an offline\n  generalize because the day's solver lacked the synthesis dispatch (see Pitfalls: it is now a 2-day repeat).\"\"\")\n# variant axes\nrep(\"\"\"1 vs TT 20 vs Mastery 100; D16 single 1 vs TT 21 vs Mastery 105 (kit + `d16-email-*`).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"1 vs TT 20 vs Mastery 100; D16 single 1 vs TT 21 vs Mastery 105 (kit + `d16-email-*`); D17 1 / 22 / 110 (+ `d17-audio-*`).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  `d14-lnk-*`, `d15-ooxml-*`, `d16-email-*`. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX; keep EVERY earlier family answerable\n  (reference: `challenges/day16/metadata-return-to-sender/solver/solve.py` answers all 21 incl. synthesis).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  `d14-lnk-*`, `d15-ooxml-*`, `d16-email-*`, `d17-audio-*`. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX; keep EVERY earlier family\n  answerable (reference: `challenges/day17/metadata-hear-me-out/solver/solve.py` answers all 22 incl. synthesis).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **fmt word vs registry key** (D16 new) -- the GM's `<fmt>` is its own word: `email.message_id` / id `dNN-email-NNN-\n  email-message-id`, while the prebuilt module registered `(\"eml\", ...)`. Rule: map fmt synonyms before lookup\n  (`email`<->`eml`, expect `mail`/`msg`/`mime`), and take the field from the slug AFTER `-NNN-<fmt>-` (or from the\n  question's `<fmt>.<field>`), never from the first occurrence of the fmt word (the id repeats it).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family word** (D16, D17) -- the GM's `<fmt>` is an abstract namespace: D16\n  `email.message_id` (prebuilt said `eml`); D17 `media.primary_audio_codec_name` with id `d17-audio-001-media-...`\n  (family word `audio`, fmt `media`; prebuilt only had `wav.*` fmt-chunk fields). Field vocabulary = ffprobe\n  (`primary_audio_` = first audio stream, `codec_name` = FFmpeg codec id). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the\n  QUESTION text (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`<->`eml`/`mime`; `media`<->`audio`/`wav`/`mp3`/\n  `mp4`/...), route the extractor by the member's MAGIC, and fall back to the same field under any fmt.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  member (`message-001.eml`) and set order re-rolls per Mastery set. `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question,\n  get_bytes, algo)` implements it -- call it from every day's solver; yesterday's `local_answer` is NOT carried over.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  member (`message-001.eml`) and set order re-rolls per Mastery set. D17: `[\"evidence-note.txt\",\"panel-001.png\",\n  \"managed-001.dll\",\"audio-001.wav\"]` -- shape so far = the note + 2 kit members (re-picked daily: jpg/exe/docx D15,\n  png/dll D17) + TODAY's new member. `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo)` implements it --\n  call it from every day's solver with get_bytes bound to the artifacts root INSIDE the per-set worker (Mastery forks\n  one process per set: a global set only in `main()` stays None -> D17 Mastery answered nothing for synthesis).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"order (driven by the re-rolled note/jpg hashes; D16 differs per set). Constant so far but d