s-siblings). Spelling unverified -> keep alternates.\"},\n {\"id\":\"flac-opus-headers\",\"concept\":\"FLAC STREAMINFO / OpusHead / Vorbis identification header fields\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt media (+flac/ogg/opus aliases), fields flac_min_block_size, flac_max_block_size, flac_sample_rate, flac_channels, flac_bits_per_sample, flac_total_samples, flac_md5_signature (32 hex, 'none' when all zero), flac_metadata_block_types, opus_version, opus_channel_count, opus_pre_skip, opus_input_sample_rate, opus_output_gain, opus_channel_mapping_family, vorbis_bitrate_nominal, vorbis_blocksizes, ogg_serial_numbers_hex, ogg_page_count, ogg_last_granule. Pure struct.\"},\n {\"id\":\"media-video-streams\",\"concept\":\"Video stream fields (codec, dimensions, frame rate, pix_fmt, rotation)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt media, fields primary_video_codec_name (h264, hevc, vp8, vp9, av1, mpeg4, mjpeg, prores), primary_video_width, primary_video_height, primary_video_dimensions_pixels ('<w>x<h>' like D4/D5), primary_video_frame_rate ('30000/1001' r_frame_rate), primary_video_pix_fmt (avcC/hvcC chroma -> yuv420p), primary_video_profile, rotation (tkhd matrix / displaymatrix), video_stream_count. MP4 stsd avc1/hvc1/hev1/vp09/av01/mp4v, MKV CodecID, AVI RIFF 'AVI ' strh/strf fourcc (H264, XVID, MJPG).\"},\n]\nfor g in new: assert g['id'] not in by, g['id']\n# re-rank existing\nfor i in ['email-fmt-alias','email-threading','email-mime-attachments','mbox-collection','email-thread-synthesis','pe-debug-rich-imports','pe-authenticode','evtx-records','regf-values','recycle-bin-i','prefetch','task-xml','ole-vba','ooxml-siblings']:\n    by[i]['priority']=2\nby['media-tags']['priority']=2\nby['media-tags']['detail']=\"BUILT as fmt wav/mp3 only (D17 GM used fmt `media`, so these were invisible) -- see media-fmt-alias. Remaining: mp4 (ftyp_major_brand, mvhd_creation_time_utc, duration_seconds) and flac (streaminfo_sample_rate, vorbis_<tag>) modules -- now covered by media-stream-fields / flac-opus-headers / media-format-tags.\"\nby['synthesis-siblings']['detail']=\"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) exists (sha256 order asked D15, D16, D17; D17 Files = note + panel-001.png + managed-001.dll + today's audio-001.wav). D16 AND D17 both timed modes went solver_incomplete because the day's solver template had no synthesis dispatch, and D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker (fork per set). The template/shared dispatch must route every `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-*` id to lib.meta.synthesis with get_bytes bound per set. Still to add there: md5/sha1/size order, duplicate groups, earliest/latest by embedded timestamp, email thread grouping, audio equivalence (media-equivalence-synthesis).\"\nby['tool-mutagen-pypdf']['detail']=\"mutagen 1.48, pypdf, exifread, soundfile are in .venv now (worker-side). Still missing: pymediainfo, PyAV. See tool-ffprobe for the media ground truth.\"\ngaps.append({\"id\":\"tool-ffprobe\",\"concept\":\"ffprobe/ffmpeg + sox for media ground truth\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"tool\",\"detail\":\"GM media fields use ffprobe vocabulary (`codec_name`, `sample_fmt`, `channel_layout`, `format_name`); ffprobe is NOT installed (mediainfo prints 'PCM'). Install a static ffmpeg build into tools/ffmpeg/ (johnvansickle amd64 static tarball, or apt ffmpeg) with a bin/ shim; worker check: `ffprobe -v error -show_streams -show_format -of json f`. Use only to verify lib struct parsers offline, never as an in-window dependency. Also apt sox (soxi).\"})\ngaps.extend(new)\norder={1:0,2:1,3:2}\n# priority-1 media first, then the rest preserving order\nmedia_first=[g['id'] for g in new if g['priority']==1]+['tool-ffprobe','synthesis-siblings','gate-allowlist-dfir-libs']\ndef key(g):\n    return (g['priority'], 0 if g['id'] in media_first else 1, media_first.index(g['id']) if g['id'] in media_first else 0)\ngaps=sorted(gaps,key=key)\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(body)\ns=s[:m.start(1)]+body+s[m.end(1):]\ns=s.replace(\"Ranking: priority 1 = plausible D17-D19 question\",\"Ranking: priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(pend),pend)\nEOF\nwc -l reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md; grep -n \"Ranking\" reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md"}}}
